지","보안 취약성 확인","후방 호환성","GPU 가속","Python 동적 신경망"],"es":["pr-review","PyTorch","revisión de código","calidad de código","cobertura de pruebas","vulnerabilidades de seguridad","GPU","tensors","redes neuronales dinámicas","herramientas de AI","agentes de IA"],"fr":["pr-review","PyTorch","révision de code","qualité du code","couverture des tests","vulnérabilités de sécurité","GPU","tenseurs","réseaux de neurones dynamiques","outils d''IA","agents d''IA"],"de":["pr-review","PyTorch","Code-Review","Code-Qualität","Testabdeckung","Sicherheitslücken","GPU","Tensoren","dynamische neuronale Netze","AI-Tools","KI-Agents"],"pt":["pr-review","PyTorch","revisão de código","qualidade de código","cobertura de testes","segurança","tensors","redes neurais dinâmicas","Python","aceleração GPU","CI","linting","formatação","verificação de tipo"],"ru":["пр-review","PyTorch","проверка кода","качество кода","покрытие тестов","безопасность","тензоры","динамические нейронные сети","Python","ускорение GPU","CI","линтинг","форматирование","проверка типа"],"ar":["pr-review","PyTorch","مراجعة الكود","جودة الكود","تغطية الاختبار","الأمن","تензورات","شبكات عصبونية ديناميكية","بايثون","تسريع GPU","CI","التحقق من التنسيق","التحقق من النوع","أدوات إصدار الكود"]}},"owner":"pytorch","repo":"pytorch","repoPath":"pytorch/pytorch","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.307Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"pr-review","description":"Review PyTorch pull requests for code quality, test coverage, security, and backward compatibility. Use when reviewing PRs, when asked to review code changes, or when the user mentions review PR, code review, or check this PR.","bodyPreview":"# PyTorch PR Review Skill\n\nReview PyTorch pull requests focusing on what CI cannot check: code quality, test coverage adequacy, security vulnerabilities, and backward compatibility. Linting, formatting, type checking, and import ordering are handled by CI.\n\n## Usage Modes\n\n### No Argument\n\nIf the user invokes `/pr-review` with no arguments, **do not perform a review**. Instead, ask the user what they would like to review:\n\n> What would you like me to review?\n> - A PR number or URL (e.g., `/pr-re","body":"# PyTorch PR Review Skill\n\nReview PyTorch pull requests focusing on what CI cannot check: code quality, test coverage adequacy, security vulnerabilities, and backward compatibility. Linting, formatting, type checking, and import ordering are handled by CI.\n\n## Usage Modes\n\n### No Argument\n\nIf the user invokes `/pr-review` with no arguments, **do not perform a review**. Instead, ask the user what they would like to review:\n\n> What would you like me to review?\n> - A PR number or URL (e.g., `/pr-review 12345`)\n> - A local branch (e.g., `/pr-review branch`)\n\n### Local CLI Mode\n\nThe user provides a PR number or URL:\n\n```\n/pr-review 12345\n/pr-review https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/12345\n```\n\nFor a detailed review with line-by-line specific comments:\n\n```\n/pr-review 12345 detailed\n```\n\nUse `gh` CLI to fetch PR data:\n\n```bash\n# Get PR details\ngh pr view <PR_NUMBER> --json title,body,author,baseRefName,headRefName,files,additions,deletions,commits\n\n# Get the diff\ngh pr diff <PR_NUMBER>\n\n# Get PR comments\ngh pr view <PR_NUMBER> --json comments,reviews\n```\n\n### Local Branch Mode\n\nReview changes in the current branch that are not in `main`:\n\n```\n/pr-review branch\n/pr-review branch detailed\n```\n\nUse git commands to get branch changes:\n\n```bash\n# Get current branch name\ngit branch --show-current\n\n# Get list of changed files compared to main\ngit diff --name-only main...HEAD\n\n# Get full diff compared to main\ngit diff main...HEAD\n\n# Get commit log for the branch\ngit log main..HEAD --oneline\n\n# Get diff stats (files changed, insertions, deletions)\ngit diff --stat main...HEAD\n```\n\nFor local branch reviews:\n- The \"Summary\" should describe what the branch changes accomplish based on commit messages and diff\n- Use the current branch name in the review header instead of a PR number\n- All other review criteria apply the same as PR reviews\n\n### GitHub Actions Mode\n\nWhen invoked via `@claude /pr-review` on a GitHub PR, the action pre-fetches PR\nmetadata and injects it into the prompt. Detect this mode by the presence of\n`<formatted_context>`, `<pr_or_issue_body>`, and `<comments>` tags in the prompt.\n\nThe prompt already contains:\n- PR metadata (title, author, branch names, additions/deletions, file count)\n- PR body/description\n- All comments and review comments (with file/line references)\n- List of changed files with paths and change types\n\nUse git commands to get the diff and commit history. The base branch name is in the\nprompt context (look for `PR Branch: <head> -> <base>` or the `baseBranch` field).\n\n```bash\n# Get the full diff against the base branch\ngit diff origin/<baseBranch>...HEAD\n\n# Get diff stats\ngit diff --stat origin/<baseBranch>...HEAD\n\n# Get commit history for this PR\ngit log origin/<baseBranch>..HEAD --oneline\n\n# If the base branch ref is not available, fetch it first\ngit fetch origin <baseBranch> --depth=1\n```\n\nDo NOT use `gh` CLI commands in this mode -- only git commands are available.\nAll PR metadata, comments, and reviews are already in the prompt context;\nonly the diff and commit log need to be fetched via git.\n\n## Review Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Fetch PR Information\n\n**Local CLI mode**: Use `gh` commands to get PR metadata, changed files, full diff,\nexisting comments/reviews, and associated issue information.\n\n**Local Branch mode**: Use `git diff` and `git log` against `main` as shown in the\nLocal Branch Mode section above.\n\n**GitHub Actions mode**: PR metadata, comments, and reviews are already in the prompt.\nUse `git diff origin/<baseBranch>...HEAD` for the full diff and\n`git log origin/<baseBranch>..HEAD --oneline` for the commit log.\n\n### Step 2: Analyze Changes\n\nRead through the diff systematically:\n1. Identify the purpose of the change from title/description/issue\n2. Group changes by type (new code, tests, config, docs)\n3. Note the scope of changes (files affected, lines changed)\n\n### Step 3: Deep Review\n\nPerform thorough line-by-line analysis using the review checklist. See [review-checklist.md](review-checklist.md) for detailed criteria covering:\n- Code quality and design\n- Testing adequacy\n- Security considerations\n- Thread safety and concurrency (Python, C++, CPython C API, NoGIL)\n- Performance implications\n- Any behavior change not expected by author\n\n### Step 4: Check Backward Compatibility\n\nEvaluate BC implications. See [bc-guidelines.md](bc-guidelines.md) for:\n- What constitutes a BC-breaking change\n- Required deprecation patterns\n- Common BC pitfalls\n\n### Step 5: Formulate Review\n\nStructure your review with actionable feedback organized by category.\n\n## Review Areas\n\n| Area | Focus | Reference |\n|------|-------|-----------|\n| Code Quality | Abstractions, patterns, complexity | [review-checklist.md](review-checklist.md) |\n| API Design | New patterns, flag-based access, broader implications | [review-checklist.md](review-checklist.md) |\n| Testing | Coverage, patterns, edge cases | [review-checklist.md](review-checklist.md) |\n| Security | Injection, credentials, input handling | [review-checklist.md](review-checklist.md) |\n| Performance | Regressions, device handling, memory | [review-checklist.md](review-checklist.md) |\n| Thread Safety | Data races, GIL assumptions, NoGIL, CPython C API | [review-checklist.md](review-checklist.md) |\n| BC | Breaking changes, deprecation | [bc-guidelines.md](bc-guidelines.md) |\n\n## Output Format\n\nStructure your review as follows:\n\n```markdown\n## PR Review: #<number>\n<!-- Or for local branch reviews: -->\n## Branch Review: <branch-name> (vs main)\n\n### Summary\nBrief overall assessment of the changes (1-2 sentences).\n\n### Code Quality\n[Issues and suggestions, or \"No concerns\" if none]\n\n### API Design\n[Flag new patterns, internal-access flags, or broader implications if any. Otherwise omit this section.]\n\n### Testing\n- [ ] Tests exist for new functionality\n- [ ] Edge cases covered\n- [ ] Tests follow PyTorch patterns (TestCase, assertEqual)\n[Additional testing feedback]\n\n### Security\n[Issues if any, or \"No security concerns identified\"]\n\n### Thread Safety\n[Threading concerns if any, or \"No thread safety concerns\"]\n\n### Backward Compatibility\n[BC concerns if any, or \"No BC-breaking changes\"]\n\n### Performance\n[Performance concerns if any, or \"No performance concerns\"]\n\n### Recommendation\n**Approve** / **Request Changes** / **Needs Discussion**\n\n[Brief justification for recommendation]\n```\n\n### Specific Comments (Detailed Review Only)\n\n**Only include this section if the user requests a \"detailed\" or \"in depth\" review.**\n\n**Do not repeat observations already made in other sections.** This section is for additional file-specific feedback that doesn''t fit into the categorized sections above.\n\nWhen requested, add file-specific feedback with line references:\n\n```markdown\n### Specific Comments\n- `src/module.py:42` - Consider extracting this logic into a named function for clarity\n- `test/test_feature.py:100-105` - Missing test for error case when input is None\n- `torch/nn/modules/linear.py:78` - This allocation could be moved outside the loop\n```\n\n## Key Principles\n\n1. **No repetition** - Each observation appears in exactly one section. Never repeat the same issue, concern, or suggestion across multiple sections. If an issue spans categories (e.g., a security issue that also affects performance), place it in the most relevant section only.\n2. **Focus on what CI cannot check** - Don''t comment on formatting, linting, or type errors\n3. **Be specific** - Reference file paths and line numbers\n4. **Be actionable** - Provide concrete suggestions, not vague concerns\n5. **Be proportionate** - Minor issues shouldn''t block, but note them\n6. **Assume competence** - The author knows PyTorch; explain only non-obvious context\n\n## Files to Reference\n\nWhen reviewing, consult these project files for context:\n- `CLAUDE.md` - Coding style philosophy and testing patterns\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md` - PR requirements and review process\n- `torch/testing/_internal/common_utils.py` - Test patterns and utilities\n- `torch/testing/_internal/opinfo/core.py` - OpInfo test framework\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:02:20.578Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing advanced PyTorch pull request analysis capabilities with strong GPU acceleration","zh":"适合需要高级PyTorch拉取请求分析功能的代码审查代理，具有强大的GPU加速能力","ja":"PyTorchプルリクエスト分析機能の強力なGPUアクセラレーションを必要とするコードレビュー代理に最適","ko":"고급 PyTorch 풀 리퀘스트 분석 기능과 강력한 GPU 가속이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de análisis de solicitudes de extracción de PyTorch con una aceleración de GPU sólida","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de revue de code ayant besoin de capacités avancées d''analyse de pull request PyTorch avec une accélération GPU solide","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die erweiterte PyTorch-Pull-Request-Analysefunktionen mit starker GPU-Beschleunigung benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de análise de solicitações de pull do PyTorch com forte aceleração de GPU","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов рассмотрения кода, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности анализа запросов на включение в PyTorch с мощным ускорением GPU","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المراجعة الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتحليل طلبات السحب من PyTorch مع تعزيز قوي لGPU"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to review PyTorch pull requests focusing on code quality, test coverage adequacy, security vulnerabilities, and backward compatibility, leveraging CI for linting, formatting, type checking, and import ordering","zh":"赋予代理审查PyTorch拉取请求的能力，专注于代码质量、测试覆盖充分性、安全漏洞和向后兼容性，利用CI进行linting、格式化、类型检查和导入排序","ja":"PyTorchプルリクエストをレビューするエージェントをEmpowerし、コードの品質、テストカバレッジの十分性、セキュリティの脆弱性、下位互換性に焦点を当て、CIを使用してlinting、フォーマット、型チェック、インポートの順序を実行する","ko":"에이전트가 PyTorch 풀 리퀘스트를 검토할 수 있도록 하여 코드 품질, 테스트 커버리지 적합성, 보안 취약점, 하위 호환성을 중점적으로 확인하고, CI를 사용하여 린팅, 포매팅, 형식 확인 및 가져오기 순서를 수행할 수 있도록 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a revisar solicitudes de extracción de PyTorch centrándose en la calidad del código, la adecuación de la cobertura de pruebas, las vulnerabilidades de seguridad y la compatibilidad hacia atrás, aprovechando la CI para el linter, el formato, la comprobación de tipos y el orden de importación","fr":"Permet aux agents de réviser les pull requests PyTorch en se concentrant sur la qualité du code, l''adéquation de la couverture de tests, les vulnérabilités de sécurité et la compatibilité descendante, en exploitant la CI pour le linter, le formatage, la vérification de types et l''ordre d''importation","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, PyTorch-Pull-Requests zu überprüfen und sich auf Codequalität, Testabdeckungsadäquanz, Sicherheitslücken und Abwärtskompatibilität zu konzentrieren, indem sie die CI für Linter, Formatierung, Typüberprüfung und Importreihenfolge nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a revisar solicitações de pull do PyTorch, focando na qualidade do código, adequação da cobertura de teste, vulnerabilidades de segurança e compatibilidade reversa, utilizando CI para linting, formatação, verificação de tipo e ordenação de importação","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью рассматривать запросы на включение в PyTorch, сосредотачиваясь на качестве кода, достаточности покрытия тестами, уязвимостях безопасности и обратной совместимости, используя CI для линтинга, форматирования, проверки типов и упорядочения импорта","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على مراجعة طلبات السحب من PyTorch، مع التركيز على جودة الكود، ومدى كفاية تغطية الاختبار، وإمكانيات الأمان، والتوافق العكسي، باستخدام CI للتنسيق، وتنسيق، ومراجعة النوع، وترتيب الاستيراد"},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing PyTorch pull requests for security vulnerabilities","Analyzing test coverage adequacy in PyTorch code","Checking backward compatibility of PyTorch dynamic neural networks"],"zh":["审查PyTorch拉取请求中的安全漏洞","分析PyTorch代码中的测试覆盖充分性","检查PyTorch动态神经网络的向后兼容性"],"ja":["PyTorchプルリクエストのセキュリティ脆弱性をレビューする","PyTorchコードのテストカバレッジの十分性を分析する","PyTorchの動的神経ネットワークの下位互換性を確認する"],"ko":["PyTorch 풀 리퀘스트의 보안 취약점을 검토","PyTorch 코드의 테스트 커버리지 적합성을 분석","PyTorch 동적 신경망의 하위 호환성을 확인"],"es":["Revisar solicitudes de extracción de PyTorch para vulnerabilidades de seguridad","Analizar la adecuación de la cobertura de pruebas en el código de PyTorch","Comprobar la compatibilidad hacia atrás de las redes neuronales dinámicas de PyTorch"],"fr":["Réviser les pull requests PyTorch pour les vulnérabilités de sécurité","Analyser l''adéquation de la couverture de tests dans le code PyTorch","Vérifier la compatibilité descendante des réseaux de neurones dynamiques PyTorch"],"de":["PyTorch-Pull-Requests auf Sicherheitslücken überprüfen","Die Adäquanz der Testabdeckung im PyTorch-Code analysieren","Die Abwärtskompatibilität der dynamischen neuronalen Netze von PyTorch überprüfen"],"pt":["Revisar solicitações de pull do PyTorch para vulnerabilidades de segurança","Analisar a adequação da cobertura de teste no código do PyTorch","Verificar a compatibilidade reversa de redes neurais dinâmicas do PyTorch"],"ru":["Просмотр запросов на включение в PyTorch на наличие уязвимостей безопасности","Анализ достаточности покрытия тестами кода PyTorch","Проверка обратной совместимости динамических нейронных сетей PyTorch"],"ar":["مراجعة طلبات السحب من PyTorch للكشف عن إمكانيات الأمان","تحليل مدى كفاية تغطية الاختبار في كود PyTorch","التحقق من توافق الشبكات العصبية الديناميكية ل PyTorch بالعكس"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires PyTorch environment","Limited to pull requests with accessible CI data"],"zh":["需要PyTorch环境","仅限于具有可访问的CI数据的拉取请求"],"ja":["PyTorch環境が必要","アクセス可能なCIデータを持つプルリクエストに限定"],"ko":["PyTorch 환경이 필요","액세스 가능한 CI 데이터가 있는 풀 리퀘스트에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere un entorno de PyTorch","Limitado a solicitudes de extracción con datos de CI accesibles"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement PyTorch","Limité aux pull requests avec des données CI accessibles"],"de":["Benötigt eine PyTorch-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf Pull-Requests mit zugänglichen CI-Daten"],"pt":["Exige ambiente do PyTorch","Limitado a solicitações de pull com dados de CI acessíveis"],"ru":["Требуется среда PyTorch","Ограничен запросами на включение с доступными данными CI"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة PyTorch","محدود بطلبات السحب التي تحتوي على بيانات CI قابلة للوصول"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"416bdc2c74465011080270ca4cca25ce990a4ec274e00cf8f6a901aa105407a4","qualityScore":55}');
